{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475668-2e-legacy-commanders-of-ephemera","id":1475668,"title":"[2e Legacy] Commanders of Ephemera","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-02T10:01:37-08:00","id":1475668,"title":"[2e Legacy] Commanders of Ephemera","content":"<b>Commanders of Ephemera</b><br /> <br /> The Commanders of Ephemera are actually three closely related legacies, each one dealing with a specific ephemeral entity: spirits, goetia, and ghosts.<br /> Most Commanders of Ephemera focus on spirits or ghosts, as those are the most plentiful ephemeral entities found \u201cin the wild\u201d; and for most of history the existence of Commanders of Ephemera focusing on goetia was mostly a hypothetical or a joke, but with Mages living in locations like Los Angeles and other cities where goetia do more regularly manifest Commanders of Ephemera focusing on goetic entities have sprung up.<br /> The Commanders of Ephemera also have many regional permutations, the legacies are an amalgam of similar traditions from all over the world rather who originally banded together for political clout within Consilia and Convocations.<br /> Commanders of Ephemera occasionally come into conflict with Werewolves, who view the Binders as poachers, or Sin-Eaters, who view the Binders as slavers.<br /> Below are the most common attainments learned by members of the legacies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Origins<br /> Parentage: </b>Obrimos, Silver Ladder or Mysterium<br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Binders, ephemerists, gym leaders (by Libertines).<br /> <b>Background:</b> occultists, spiritualists, ghost hunters, clergy.<br /> <b>Appearances: </b>Religious garb is common, as are symbols or clothes that evoke rulership or leadership.<br /> <br /> <b>Doctrine<br /> Prerequisites: </b>Spirit/Death/Mind 2, a Familiar of the type appropriate to the chosen Arcanum, Occult 2, and one of the following skills at 2 dots or higher: Empathy, Persuasion, Politics, Intimidation, or Expression.<br /> <b>Initiation:</b> Initiates must prove they are capable of controlling the appropriate ephemeral entity and making it submit to their will: some masters are fine with a pupil \u201ctaming\u201d a placid entity, where others demand the pupil and the pupil\u2019s familiar(s) dominate the entity by force.<br /> <b>Organization: </b>The Legacy is primarily a master/student relationship, though members of one \u201cbranch\u201d will recommend prospective candidates for another.<br /> <b>Theory: </b>The ephemeral realms are always beside us, replete with Mystery and capable entities, those entities should be harnessed for the good of humanity and we, with our connection to Truth, are the best equipped to do so.<br /> <br /> <b>Magic<br /> Ruling Arcanum:</b> Spirit <i>or</i> Death <i>or </i>Mind<br /> <b>Yantras:</b> religious symbols or symbols of leadership (+1), salt (+1), incense filled room (+2), chanting a prayer or issuing commands (+2, cannot be used reflexively).<br /> <b>Oblations:</b> ritual purification of oneself or a site, leading a meeting or holding court.<br /> <br /> <b>Attainments</b><br /> <b>First: </b>The Invisible Revealed<br /> <b>Prerequisite: </b>Initiation<br /> The Binder can always sense the entities of their focus, this Attainment acts as <i>Exorcist\u2019s Eye</i> with reach spent on Advanced Duration, but is keyed to only entities of the appropriate type for the Ruling Arcanum gained from the Legacy.<br /> <b>Optional: </b>Prime 1<br /> The Binder always knows the direction and distance to the nearest source of Essence appropriate to the type of entity on which they focus as well as the resonance of that Essence. By concentrating for a turn the Binder can tune to a specific resonance rather than just looking for Essence in general.<br /> <br /> <b>Second:</b> Divine Protection<br /> <b>Prerequisite: </b>Spirit/Death/Mind 2, Occult 3<br /> The powers of ephemeral entities are often dangerous, this Attainment wards the Binder from the powers of the ephemeral entities they are most likely to encounter. This Attainment acts as <i>Mental Shield</i>, <i>Ghost Shield</i>, or <i>Ephemeral Shield</i> as appropriate with reach assigned to Advanced Duration. This attainment also affects a number of the Binder\u2019s familiars equal to half their dots in Spirit/Death/Mind (rounded down).<br /> <b>Optional: </b>Prime 2<br /> The resilience of a Binder\u2019s shield against their brand of ephemeral target is unparalleled. Even should the initial Clash go in the attacking entity\u2019s favor the Binder can activate Prime Mage Armor against a damaging attack without having to spend a point of Mana or can attempt a second Clash of Wills on their next turn if the spell has an ongoing effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Third: </b>Flesh over Ephemera<br /> <b>Prerequisite: </b>Spirit/Death/Mind 3, Occult 3, a Rank 2 familiar<br /> The Binder can equip their ephemeral entities with tools capable of affecting those not in Twilight or make it so their own tools work on entities in Twilight. With a scene long ritual the Binder attunes an item to the frequency of Twilight for the appropriate ephemeral entity for a duration equal to their dots in Spirit/Death/Mind on the Advanced Duration chart; when the item is corporeal it fully affects Twilight entities of the appropriate type, when in Twilight it can be used on corporeal objects and people. Items enhanced via this Attainment that are in Twilight can be seen by those without the ability to see ephemeral entities with a Wits + Composure - the Binder\u2019s Spirit/Death/Mind. Items under the effects of this Attainment do not lose their material form when taken into Twilight, the Shadow, the Underworld, or the Astral (as appropriate).<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Prime 3<br /> Items altered by the primary Attainment work on all ephemeral entities, rather than just those of the appropriate type.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth:</b> As I Will<br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Spirit/Death/Mind 4. In addition to the Occult 3 requirement from the previous Attainment, the Exorcist must increase the other Skill used to meet the prerequisites of the Legacy to 3, or must attain 2 dots in a second skill from the list of possible requirements.<br /> The Binder speaks and ephemeral entities obey. This Attainment acts as <i>Command Spirit/Ghost/Goetia</i> with reach assigned to Instant cast, Advanced Duration, and Sensory Range and potency equal to Spirit/Death/Mind.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Prime 4<br /> A Binder at this level can use their familiar as a potent magical item. A Binder can spend a scene to bind a spell to their familiar as if creating an Imbue Item (removing or swapping the Imbued spell likewise requires a scene). The Imbued spell does not take up the Binder\u2019s spell control, and the familiar can hold a number of spells equal to the Binder\u2019s Prime dots via this attainment; if the Binder has more than one familiar than the total number of spells across all familiars is limited by the Binder\u2019s Prime dots. The familiar is <i>not</i> limited to having only one Contingent spell imbued.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth:</b> Ephemeral Master<br /> <b>Prerequisite: </b>Spirit/Death/Mind 5, Occult 4.<br /> The Binder\u2019s familiar becomes Rank 3 but still retains the familiar manifestation; if a Binder has more than one familiar then only one becomes Rank 3 immediately, but the Binder can have a number of Rank 3 familiars equal to their dots in Spirit/Death/Mind. Additionally, the Binder can spend a point of Mana to gain dots in Status towards ephemeral entities of the appropriate type for a scene equal to their dots in Spirit/Death/Mind; if a powerful (rank 4+) entity already holds sway over the area then this Attainment can be contested with a Clash of Wills.<br /> <b>Optional: </b>Prime 5<br /> Should the Binder so desire, the entire area loses its distinction between physical and Twilight, everything is treated as fully solid. This Attainment mimics the effects of the spell <i>Ephemeral Enchantment</i> with Instant cast, Advanced Duration, and Advanced Scale: Area.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T13:43:52-08:00","id":1475680,"title":"","content":"My only complaint is that fluff-wise they\u2019re rather generic compared to other Legacies like the Clavicularius. But the attainments are solidly written. I approve. <br /> <br /> Of course, the logical conclusion of having variations for different flavors of ephemera would be a Fate-primary version that goes after angels \ud83d\ude1b (the attainments would require conjunctional Prime).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T15:32:55-08:00","id":1475687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475668-2e-legacy-commanders-of-ephemera?p=1475680#post1475680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only complaint is that fluff-wise they\u2019re rather generic compared to other Legacies like the Clavicularius. But the attainments are solidly written. I approve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, unfortunately really nailing down a solid flavor on something spanning three potential primary Arcana (or more!) is a bit difficult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, the logical conclusion of having variations for different flavors of ephemera would be a Fate-primary version that goes after angels \ud83d\ude1b (the attainments would require conjunctional Prime). </div> </div> </div>The only issue there is you can't force G-M &quot;angels&quot; to go against the G-M, but if there were a location with a high density of G-M &quot;angels&quot; then such a branch might develop like the Commanders of Goetia developed in places like Los Angeles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T02:05:10-08:00","id":1475726,"title":"","content":"Speaking of solid flavor, I think you should take the monicker of &quot;Gym Leaders&quot; and just run with it. Commanders would take ephemerals under their wing, developing a mutually challenging relationship. They would train their wards, but also train themselves to remain worthy of loyalty. This could take the form of a journey or intensive training in a fighting dojo. It would be a very Adamantine Arrow philosophy. You could crib liberally from Pokemon, with the added benefit of exploring aspects that the franchise glosses over. For instance, are you truly the best, if only your wards improve? How do their particular needs alter the trajectory of development for a trainer? Do Commanders that stay in the back, shouting orders, breed resentment in their 'Mons? You can deconstruct and reconstruct beloved games and cartoons, so there's real heft to than concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T02:28:21-08:00","id":1475727,"title":"","content":"Heheh, Gym Leaders \u2014 gotta agree with Teatime above on that one.<br /> <br /> We could even do TMs and HMs via spells that copy and transfer Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T02:35:07-08:00","id":1475728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475668-2e-legacy-commanders-of-ephemera?p=1475727#post1475727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We could even do TMs and HMs via spells that copy and transfer Numina.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. I like this a lot. Especially since it carries a risk of accidentally creating a Magath, or an outright Ghost/Spirit/Angel/Goetia hybrid.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T17:37:52-08:00","id":1475756,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't a Rank 3 ghost familiar already be a Geist ? In such a case, wouldn't there be an ever present risk of them terminating the familiar bond in favor of striking the Bargain ? Because at the end of the day, ghosts have a strong fixation with whatever business they had with the living and a Bound might let them experience it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T18:27:54-08:00","id":1475757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475668-2e-legacy-commanders-of-ephemera?p=1475756#post1475756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't a Rank 3 ghost familiar already be a Geist ? In such a case, wouldn't there be an ever present risk of them terminating the familiar bond in favor of striking the Bargain ? Because at the end of the day, ghosts have a strong fixation with whatever business they had with the living and a Bound might let them experience it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say that external sources of power, Supernal or otherwise, can exalt a ghost to Rank 3+ without the transformation into a Geist/Reaper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}